# mario-party-superstars — example configuration.
# Copy to ".env" and fill in real values. NEVER commit your real .env.

# --- MPS NEX identity ---
# CONFIRMED (2026-08-18) via brute-force against a real captured PRUDP signature --
# mathematically certain, not inferred. See README.md and main.go's defaultAccessKey
# comment for the full story (the DNS-resolve hostname's hex value, 28abaa00, turned
# out to be the Game Server ID, a DIFFERENT value from the real access key below).
MPS_ACCESS_KEY=e915510f
# CONFIRMED via direct binary inspection of the same dump -- main's .rodata carries
# "SDK MW+Nintendo+NEX-4_6_5-" in its SDK-build-version string table. Real data, not a
# guess, unlike the access key above.
MPS_NEX_VERSION=40605

# --- Wire-shape knobs ---
# Station URL scheme handed back by auth. "prudps" makes the console send its Kerberos
# ticket in CONNECT; "prudp" completes the handshake but sends an EMPTY CONNECT payload.
MPS_STATION_SCHEME=prudps
# PRUDP minor version answered in the SECURE endpoint's SYN-ACK. Never applied to auth.
MPS_SECURE_MINOR=0
# CONFIRMED Pia 5.33.0 (same dump, same string table) -- well past the 5.19 that
# introduced the modern shape, so 0 (modern, type=0x0B + Pa) is solid here, not a guess.
# Kept overridable in case Pia changed shape again between 5.19 and 5.33 -- untested.
MPS_LEGACY_PIA=0

# --- Network ---
# BARE IP the console will dial. NOT host:port — this becomes the station URL's "address"
# param and the port is set separately from SECURE_PORT. Set this to your own server's real
# public IP.
NEXTENDO_HOST=127.0.0.1
AUTH_PORT=8452
SECURE_PORT=60012
NEXTENDO_PROXY_PROTOCOL=0

# --- TLS (both endpoints terminate TLS themselves) ---
CERT_FILE=cert.pem
KEY_FILE=key.pem

# --- Nextendo account integration ---
# Local testing: point at a port that refuses INSTANTLY. The gate client has a 3 s timeout
# and fails OPEN, so an unresolvable host silently adds ~3 s to every login.
NEXTENDO_ACCOUNT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:1
NEXTENDO_REQUIRE_ACCOUNT=0
NEXTENDO_REQUIRE_SIGNED_TOKEN=0

# --- Monitoring ---
# The dashboard is FAIL-CLOSED: with no token every /api request gets 403.
# 8088 -- next free slot after smm2's 8085 in the VPS's live port table.
DASH_PORT=8088
DASH_TOKEN=change-me
# Cosmetic only — displayed in /api/stats.
NEXTENDO_SNI_HOST=g28abaa00

# --- Secrets (set these to strong random values in production) ---
NEXTENDO_INTERNAL_KEY=
# Token-signing secret: set the value directly...
NEXTENDO_SECRET=
# ...or point to a file that holds it (default: nextendo_secret.key next to the binary).
NEXTENDO_SECRET_FILE=
# Kerberos password shared between the auth and secure endpoints.
NEXTENDO_SECURE_PASSWORD=securepasswordplz1

# Embedded friend-directory fallback (see friends.go) -- real account service /internal/npln-friends
# 404s in production tonight (systemic, confirmed same on ARMS/LM3), so without this mm.FriendPIDs
# always answers "no friends" and the in-game Join Room screen never gets a live gid to poll.
MPS_FRIENDS_FILE=
